---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import LegalPageShell from "@/components/LegalPageShell.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How SeenTube and Arigato Labs collect, use, and protect your data."
>
  <LegalPageShell
    title="Privacy Policy"
    lead="Plain-language summary of what SeenTube stores and why."
    updated="August 2026"
  >
    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>SeenTube</strong> is a product of <strong>Arigato Labs</strong>, founded by Kumar Devanshu.
        Contact: <a href="mailto:kumardevanshu3001@gmail.com">kumardevanshu3001@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Account:</strong> name, email, and profile photo from Google sign-in (Firebase Authentication).</li>
        <li><strong>Profile:</strong> your chosen username and optional category preferences.</li>
        <li><strong>App content you create:</strong> saved videos, tags, descriptions, watch statuses, roadmaps, and connection requests.</li>
        <li><strong>Security settings:</strong> your One Password question in plain text and a salted hash of your answer (never the plain answer) for protected deletes.</li>
        <li><strong>Local device data:</strong> short-lived caches and signed-in flags in browser storage to keep the app fast across page loads.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical:</strong> standard hosting/request logs from our host (Vercel) and Firebase may include IP and basic device metadata as part of normal service operation.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2>3. How we use data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide SeenTube features: collections, Guild sharing, roadmaps, and exports.</li>
        <li>Keep you signed in and sync your data across devices.</li>
        <li>Protect destructive actions with One Password verification.</li>
        <li>Improve reliability and fix abuse or security issues.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2>4. Third parties</h2>
      <p>We use these services to run SeenTube. We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal data.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Google / Firebase</strong> — authentication and Firestore database.</li>
        <li><strong>Vercel</strong> — app hosting and serverless API routes.</li>
        <li><strong>YouTube</strong> — public video metadata (title/thumbnail) when you paste a link; we do not use a YouTube Data API key for browsing your private watch history.</li>
        <li><strong>Web3Forms</strong> (if configured) — delivers Contact form messages to the founder email.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Each provider processes data under their own policies.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2>5. Storage &amp; retention</h2>
      <p>
        Account and app content live in Firebase (cloud). Browser caches are temporary and local.
        You can remove videos and roadmaps you own (with One Password). Connection and username
        data remain while your account is active. For a full account wipe request, email
        <a href="mailto:kumardevanshu3001@gmail.com">kumardevanshu3001@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2>6. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use signed-in access, Firestore security rules, server-verified tokens for sensitive APIs,
        and hashed One Password answers. No system is perfect — please use a strong Google account
        and a memorable but private security answer.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2>7. Children</h2>
      <p>SeenTube is not directed at children under 13. Do not create an account if you are under 13.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2>8. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy. Continued use of SeenTube after changes means you accept the updated version.
        The “Last updated” date at the top will change when we revise it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2>9. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions: <a href="mailto:kumardevanshu3001@gmail.com">kumardevanshu3001@gmail.com</a>
        or the <a href="/contact">Contact</a> page.
      </p>
    </section>
  </LegalPageShell>
</Layout>
